go 1.26.6

use (
	.
	./anubiskit
)

// go-kit v0.13.0 requires the pre-split google.golang.org/genproto, which still
// carries googleapis/rpc. Standalone that is harmless — the longer module path,
// google.golang.org/genproto/googleapis/rpc, wins for the packages beneath it —
// but a workspace resolves one build list across every module in it, and there
// grpc/status finds the package in both and refuses to choose.
//
// So the pin lives HERE rather than in anubiskit/go.mod. It is a property of
// this workspace, not of the published module, and a replace in a published
// module is ignored by consumers anyway. Moving it out is what let anubiskit be
// tagged at all; release.yml checks the module still resolves with GOWORK=off.
replace google.golang.org/genproto => google.golang.org/genproto v0.0.0-20260810153831-ec0a7760b754
